		{
			dependencies: ["1F3E4F7584A6D25E"]
			description: [
				"The Eye has led you to the sanctuary, but the hall is silent. The Night Warden stands before you, not as a guardian, but as a statue of sorrow, locked in a deep, stony slumber. He is a shell that moves no more, bound by a promise that has outlived his own soul."
				""
				"To free him, you must find the Excrucis."
				""
				"It lies within the cathedral shadows, a twisted artifact that pulses with the potential for a ritual. The inscription whispers that it can \"save someone,\" but do not be deceived by the softness of that word. For a being such as this, salvation is not a healing hand; it is the release of death."
				""
				"You must perform the ritual. Use the Excrucis to pierce his slumber. But be warned: he will not wake gently."
				""
				"When his eyes open, the void will scream. He will fight you with the desperation of a man who has forgotten how to die. He will shift his form, first raining magic upon you, then hunting you with lethal melee strikes, and finally merging both in a chaotic storm. Do not rely on a single element, for he adapts to your attacks. Bring the full breadth of your magical knowledge, at least three schools of sorcery, or your spells will shatter against his resolve."
				""
				"Watch the shadows. If he teleports twice, dodge instantly to evade his scythe. And when he begins to channel the dying star to obliterate you, have your counterspells ready. You must extinguish his light before it goes supernova."
				""
				"Awake him, traveler. And then, grant him the end he has earned."
			]
			hide_until_deps_complete: true
